From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 18:32:49 +0400
Subject: [PATCH] Meridian: Boost's Improve is one button again: the site less
 distracting in one quick round, what it hides named Zaps
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The owner: 1.5.2's Improve "отлично срабатывала"; 1.5.3's was slow and
unclear. 1.5.3 made Improve with nothing typed a redesign: up to three
rounds, each with a screenshot (one JPEG, ~38 KB of base64) and a
measured page and designer brief (14 KB of text against 1.5.2's 10 KB),
the whole CSS written each round. In the beta's narrow panel the field
was cut off and the button, in a pale space's colour, looked disabled.

Now, as in 1.5.2 and simpler:
- One button, nothing to type: "Declutter" («Убрать лишнее» in Russian).
  One quick round with 1.5.2's prompt shape (the outline, the boost's CSS)
  and a fixed direction: the site less distracting (Shorts and reels
  shelves, badges and counters, promo, sign-up and cookie banners,
  autoplay rails, sticky popups), labels in the browser's language. No
  screenshot, no review, no redesign.
- What it hides becomes the site's Zaps, each with its name
  ("ytd-rich-shelf-renderer[is-shorts] /* the Shorts shelf */"): the Zap
  list shows the name, a click shows it on the page for a moment, its ✕
  brings it back by itself. "Undo all" puts the boost back as it was.
- It says what it does from the click (the first line in under a
  millisecond in the page), line by line: "Looking at the page…",
  "Asking Claude Code… read 812 elements of the page", "Found: …",
  then "Hid: the Shorts shelf, the notification count". The button is a
  strong blue whatever the space's colour, pressed while it works, never
  greyed out: with no AI it says why and opens Settings › AI.
- The AIs on this computer are waited for (WhenDetected) instead of
  failing a first Improve; where the time goes is logged (MERIDIAN_LOG:
  "Meridian Improve: quick, 1 round(s), 10755 prompt bytes,
  0 screenshot(s); … AI answering 1553 ms, first CSS at 1556 ms").
- The redesign in rounds stays as an engine for Remix
  (BoostImprover::Start(…, Mode::kRedesign), Keep(), progress(),
  changes_json(); boost_magic.ts its glow); Boost no longer uses it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
